  "description": "T-3631 (decision 0225): invariant cells of RAND (column A) and RANDBETWEEN (column B), whose value does not depend on the draw, for Gate B. Why each form is invariant: RAND is in [0,1), so a comparison with a bound outside or at the edge of that interval (RAND()<1, RAND()>=0, RAND()-RAND()<1, SUM of two draws < 2, RAND()^1<1), a product with 0, a draw compared with itself through LET (one draw), and IF/IFS/SWITCH/CHOOSE whose chosen branch does not use the draw give one value for every draw. RANDBETWEEN with equal whole bounds, or bounds whose CEILING(bottom) is at or above FLOOR(top) (5.5..5.7, -5.5..-5.2, 0.5..0.9, -2.5..-2.5, 2.0000001..2.9), has one possible result; number text, booleans, blanks, errors and bottom > top are argument checks made before any draw; the LET forms test integer-ness and range of one draw (OR over every possible value, AND of the bounds); x*0, sums of degenerate draws and SUM/INDEX over arrays of degenerate bounds do not depend on the draw. B24 and B31 take MAX and MIN over 1000 draws of RANDBETWEEN(1E15,1E15), where the double spacing is 0.125: a draw computed as bottom + r without a clamp to top would round to 1E15+1 for r >= 0.9375, so 1000 draws would show it with near certainty (0.9375^1000 < 1E-28) instead of one draw missing it.",
  "tags": [
    "M5",
    "volatile",
    "probe"
  ],
